-- A defaulted threshold pressure between two equilibration regions in a
-- compositional run.  The column of MULTZ_BARRIER without the barrier: 20
-- cells split into two blocks of ten, each its own equilibration region, the
-- upper block equilibrated at 250 bar and the lower at 155 bar, each with a
-- water zone at its base.
--
-- THPRES gives no value for the two regions, so the threshold is the largest
-- potential difference between them in the initial state: that of the water,
-- about 98 bar from layer 10 down to layer 11.  No potential difference ever
-- exceeds it, so no fluid crosses the boundary, and both blocks stay at rest
-- in their equilibrated states.  Without THPRES the blocks equalise within the
-- first report step.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
   A DEFAULTED THRESHOLD PRESSURE BETWEEN TWO COMPOSITIONAL BLOCKS

METRIC

TABDIMS
/
OIL
GAS
WATER
DIMENS
1 1 20 /

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP /

START
  1 'JAN' 2016  /

REGDIMS
1 1 0 0 /

EQLDIMS
2 200 /

EQLOPTS
'THPRES' /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

------------------------------------------------------------------------
GRID
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/grid.inc' /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROPS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/props.inc' /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
REGIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
EQLNUM
10*1 10*2
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOLUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The water-oil contact of each block lies three layers above its base.
EQUIL
   2010  250  2035  0  2000  0  /
   2060  155  2085  0  2050  0  /

-- No value: the threshold follows from the equilibrated state.
THPRES
 1 2 /
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/summary.inc' /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCHEDULE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/schedule.inc' /

END
